    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "around a long time. I think Kevin brought us the majority. He was a very prolific fundraiser for the Republicans in the house. And I think when you're not in charge, I think he's probably had enough and wants to move on. But I wish him well. And he has served our nation from California for a number of years. And I'm sure he will do beyond to other things. He said he's going to continue to fight to save our country and to promote conservative values. But that's about where that stands. But a lot of people that, you know, one thing people don't realize, Joe, is that the Republicans in the House of Representatives have term limits on leadership. Now, Kevin was term limited in quite an unusual way, the only person ever, only speaker ever. But we have term limits on leadership. You can only serve as leader, either ranker or chair of a committee for six years. And once that's done, you can no longer serve as chair on that committee. So people often retire after that, which is Patrick McHenry, who is the chair of the financial services committee, is in his last term as leader, and he's leaving. And that is very common. That's why you see so much turnover in the Republican Party and almost none in the Democratic Party. They don't do term limits. They don't believe in changing leadership. You have the same people really for 20 and 30 and 40 years serving in Congress and serving in leadership. We don't do that. We bring in new people and fresh blood, and I think it's better and healthier for our conference, but it's a challenging time indeed. I think Speaker Johnson has got a very big challenge ahead of him. He's a very good man. He's a good friend of mine. He's very conservative. He's a spiritual guy and he's practical. And I think that's the person we need to lead us right now. Congresswoman Claudia Tenney, thank you so much for joining me today and throughout the year. I hope you have a great holiday and we'll speak in 2024. Yeah, thanks so much Joe and Mary Christmas and Happy Holidays to everyone.",
